window.LESSONS = {"daily-brief":{"title":"Guided lesson — The daily brief agent: seven steps around the AI-native SDLC","guideUrl":"https://github.com/RyanLisse/aetherlink-training-site/blob/main/agents/daily-brief/LESSON.md","participantRepo":"https://github.com/RyanLisse/aetherlink-training-site/tree/main/agents/daily-brief","slides":[
{"title":"Welcome · the daily brief agent","kicker":"GUIDED LESSON · DAILY BRIEF AGENT · 10:00–10:10","subtitle":"One agent, built step by step: intent, spec, design, plan, build, evidence, gate. Individually or as a MOB.","cards":[{"title":"Outcome","body":"One agent around the loop in seven steps, one document or file per step, through a human gate."},{"title":"Scenario","body":"An agent reads GitLab, Jira, Confluence and Outlook every morning and writes a one-page brief."},{"title":"Boundary","body":"Sample data only, no credential anywhere. The lab starts empty; your branch is yours."}],"prompt":"Open out/latest.html from the reference solution and read the brief aloud: greeting, push, to-dos, updates, your day. Ask: which of these lines would you trust, and what would you need to see to trust the rest? That question is the whole day.","notes":"Welkom. Laat eerst het eindresultaat zien (de brief), dan pas de lege lab-repo. Zeg expliciet: vandaag géén echte credentials. De lab-repo begint leeg; per stap één document of bestand. Vier concepten komen terug: AI-native SDLC, agentic loop, hooks, human gate.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Outcome: Everyone has walked one agent around the loop in seven steps, each step leaving a document or a file, and taken it through a human gate\n• Scenario: An agent that reads GitLab, Jira, Confluence and the Outlook calendar every morning and writes a one-page brief in the style of two reference PDFs\n• Boundary: Sample data only; no credential in a prompt or a commit; the lab repository starts empty and your branch is yours","dark":true,"steps":["Show the finished brief.","Show the empty lab: main has templates only.","Name the four concepts.","Confirm the boundary: sample data only."],"expected":"Everyone has seen the finished artifact and the empty start before the first step.","check":"Everyone can say what the agent produces and what it may never touch.","layout":"cards","tagline":"SEVEN STEPS · SEVEN ARTIFACTS · ONE LOOP","concepts":["AI-native SDLC — the loop","The agentic loop inside query()","Hooks — where the guardrails hold","Human gate — intent, plan, pull request"]},
{"title":"Lesson route","kicker":"FIXED SCHEDULE · 10:00–16:00","subtitle":"Seven steps on the loop, each with a tag in the lab to compare against.","cards":[{"title":"Morning","body":"10:00–10:15 welcome · 10:15–10:35 concept: the loop · 10:35–11:10 step 1 intent · 11:10–11:20 step 2 spec · 11:20–11:35 break"},{"title":"Midday","body":"11:35–12:00 step 2 practice · 12:00–13:00 lunch · 13:00–13:25 step 3 design and plan · 13:25–14:00 step 4 render"},{"title":"Afternoon","body":"14:00–14:15 step 5 the loop · 14:15–14:30 break · 14:30–15:00 step 5 demo and tool · 15:00–15:20 hooks and evidence · 15:20–15:35 step 7 gate · 15:35–16:00 deploy, transfer, close"}],"prompt":"Read the route aloud. For the next block, name the step, the document or file it produces, the tag in the lab that holds the reference (step-1-intent … step-7-gate-deploy), and the human check that closes it.","notes":"Houd lunch en de twee pauzes vast; schuif de inhoud, niet de grenzen. Elke stap heeft een tag in de lab-repo: deelnemers vergelijken met `git diff step-N-… -- <bestand>`.","dark":false,"steps":["Name the seven steps in order.","Name the tag of the next step.","Confirm lunch and the breaks."],"expected":"Everyone knows which artifact ends each step and where the reference lives.","check":"Board matches the guide.","layout":"cards","tagline":"SAME RHYTHM · CONCEPT FIRST · INDIVIDUAL AFTER · GATE BEFORE THE NEXT STEP"},
{"title":"What is an AI-native SDLC?","kicker":"CONCEPT DEFINITION · AI-NATIVE SDLC","subtitle":"The same control objectives, new enforcement: the line becomes a loop and AI is embedded at every point.","cards":[{"title":"FROM LINE TO LOOP","body":"Plan → Design → Build → Test → Deploy → Maintain, and what production teaches re-enters the plan."},{"title":"AI AT EVERY POINT","body":"AI drafts, generates, reviews first, tests and watches. Humans set intent, judge risk and own the release."},{"title":"SAME CONTROLS, NEW ENFORCEMENT","body":"Quality, security and traceability stay. They move from checklists and sign-offs into the pipeline."}],"prompt":"Read the definition out loud, word for word. Then ask: in this lab, where does quality live? (spec.md and brief.ts.) Where does security live? (tools: [], read-only sources, esc().) Where does traceability live? (evidence.md, gate.md, the PR.)","notes":"Vaste cadans: definitie → beeld → hoe wij ermee werken. Lees de definitie letterlijk voor; laat de groep de drie controls zelf op een bestand plakken.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• From line to loop: Plan → Design → Build → Test → Deploy → Maintain, and what production teaches re-enters the plan. For this agent: tomorrow's brief reads what today's merge changed.\n• AI at every point: AI drafts, generates, reviews first, tests and watches. Humans set intent, judge risk and own the release. Today Claude drafts every document and every file; you accept, cut and decide.\n• Same controls, new enforcement: Quality, security and traceability stay. Here they live in a spec that quotes its source, a schema the model cannot escape, a test suite, an evidence log and a pull request, not in a checklist.","dark":false,"steps":["Name the six phases.","Place quality, security and traceability on a file each."],"expected":"The room can say \"same objectives, new enforcement\" and point at a file for each objective.","check":"Every control objective has a file, not a meeting, behind it.","layout":"cards"},
{"title":"The brief on the loop · see it","kicker":"VISUAL · AI-NATIVE SDLC","subtitle":"Six phases, one document or file each, two human gates and one hook point.","cards":[],"prompt":"Point at each phase and name its document or file. Then point at the two orange gates and ask who sits there. Then the purple mark: what holds without asking anyone?","notes":"Wijs de artefacten aan: intent.md, spec.md, plan.md; design.md, ADR, brief.ts; render.ts, sources.ts, agent.ts; npm test, sample-run, evidence.md; gate.md, PR, schedule; notes-voetnoot, progress.md. Oranje = mens beslist. Paars = code houdt zonder te vragen.","dark":false,"steps":["Name the document or file of each phase.","Say who sits at each orange gate."],"expected":"Everyone can walk the loop naming a file per phase.","check":"Nobody places a human approval prompt inside the build phase.","layout":"image","image":"daily-brief-on-the-loop.svg","imageAlt":"Six phases on an orange loop, each with the daily brief agent's documents and files: intent, spec and plan; design, ADR and brief.ts; render, sources and agent; npm test, the sample run and evidence.md; gate.md, the merged PR and a schedule; the notes footnote and progress.md. Two orange human gates and one purple hook point sit on the loop around the Claude Agent SDK.","imageCaption":"The loop is not a metaphor here: tomorrow's brief reads today's merge. Orange marks are where a human decides; the purple mark is where code holds without asking."},
{"title":"The brief on the loop · how we use it","kicker":"HOW WE USE IT · AI-NATIVE SDLC","subtitle":"Per step: what you write in the lab, and the decision that stays yours.","cards":[],"prompt":"Walk the seven rows with the lab repository open at the solution branch. For each row, open the file and show the line that proves it. Then ask everyone to pick the row where their own team would most want the human decision to stay.","notes":"Open de lab-repo op de solution-branch naast de slide. Per rij één bestand, één regel. Laat de groep de rij kiezen waar hún team de mens wil houden.","dark":false,"steps":["Open the file for each row.","Pick the row your team would keep human."],"expected":"Every participant has mapped one step to a file and a human decision.","check":"Nobody names a step where the human has no decision.","layout":"compare","columns":[{"title":"You write","items":["1 Plan · intent.md: outcome, success checks, boundary, OPEN","2 Plan · docs/spec.md quoting the PDFs, brief.ts, the sample, schema tests","3 Design · docs/design.md, ADR-001, docs/plan.md with proof commands","4 Build · render.ts and a sample-only main.ts: the first artifact","5 Build · sources.ts and agent.ts: read-only tools and one query()","6 Test · docs/evidence.md: three commands, one screenshot, one reviewer","7 Deploy · docs/gate.md and the schedule"],"foot":"AI drafts, you cut"},{"title":"Stays human","items":["1 · the boundary: what the agent may never touch","2 · which fields exist and what the reference justifies","3 · which option wins in the ADR and when the plan is accepted","4 · whether the page matches the PDFs","5 · which sources are allowed; that the model gets no shell","6 · signing as reviewer only for what you reran","7 · PASS / FAIL / OPEN, read against intent.md"],"foot":"Humans decide at every gate"}]},
{"title":"Step 1 · read the intent","kicker":"DEMO · 10:35–10:45 · 10 MIN","subtitle":"intent.md is the human starting brief: what, why, boundaries, and what is still OPEN","cards":[{"title":"What","body":"A one-page morning brief from the team's own systems, rendered as a self-contained HTML artifact"},{"title":"Why","body":"Fifteen minutes a day go to five tabs. The agent does the reading; the judging stays human."},{"title":"Boundaries","body":"Read-only tokens, no shell, no invented facts, an honest footnote when a source is silent. OPEN: mailbox, projects."}],"prompt":"Open intent.md at tag step-1-intent next to the empty template on main. Read outcome, success checks and OPEN. Point at the checks the sample run already proves and the two that need a live run. Say why OPEN is not a gap.","notes":"Toon de lege template op main en de ingevulde versie op de tag naast elkaar. Benadruk: OPEN is een eerlijke vraag, geen gat. De success checks worden later de tests.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Why: The first fifteen minutes of every day go to five tabs; the brief moves that reading to an agent and leaves the judging to the person\n• Boundaries: Read-only tokens, no shell for the model, no invented facts, an honest footnote when a source is silent; OPEN: which mailbox, which projects, which language","dark":false,"steps":["Show the template and the filled intent side by side.","Read outcome and success checks.","Read the OPEN list."],"expected":"Everyone can name one success check and one OPEN item.","check":"Nobody treats an OPEN item as decided.","layout":"cards","tagline":"WHAT · WHY · BOUNDARIES · OPEN IS WRITTEN DOWN, NOT GUESSED"},
{"title":"Practice · step 1 · write the intent","kicker":"PRACTICE · 10:45–11:00 · 15 MIN · SOLO OR MOB","subtitle":"Card 1 · plan: fill intent.md on your own branch, unknowns as OPEN","cards":[{"title":"Goal","body":"intent.md: one-sentence outcome, three checks a fresh reader can verify, boundary, owners, one OPEN."},{"title":"Input","body":"The template on main; the finished brief you saw at 10:00; reference/ with the two PDFs"},{"title":"Result","body":"intent.md committed on my/<name>; every unknown as an OPEN line, not a guess"}],"prompt":"Act as an intent interviewer for the daily brief agent in this repository. Ask one question at a time until we can state the outcome, three verifiable success checks, the boundary (what the agent may never do), the owners and the open questions. Then fill intent.md in place, keeping every unknown as an OPEN line. Do not write code, do not touch docs/, do not add a source we did not name.","notes":"15 minuten alleen. De prompt laat Claude Code interviewen en invullen; de deelnemer streept en kort in. Geen code. Wat niemand weet is OPEN.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Goal: intent.md filled: outcome in one sentence, three success checks a fresh reader can verify, boundary, owners, at least one OPEN\n\nModus: individueel (ieder op my/<naam>) óf MOB (groepjes van 3–4, één driver, navigator wisselt elke 5–7 minuten, branch mob/<groep>). Kies per sessie; de stap, de tag en de check blijven gelijk.","dark":false,"steps":["git switch -c my/<name>.","Run the interview prompt; answer one question at a time.","Cut the draft to one outcome and three checks.","Mark every unknown OPEN; commit."],"expected":"intent.md with three verifiable success checks and at least one OPEN, committed.","check":"No success check needs the author in the room to be verified.","layout":"exercise","timer":15,"mascot":true,"tagline":"YOUR TURN · 15 MINUTES · NO CODE YET"},
{"dark":false,"layout":"image","cards":[],"notes":"Herhaling in beeld. Wijs het plaatje aan en laat de groep het concept in één zin zeggen.","title":"Human gate · see the decision","kicker":"VISUAL · HUMAN GATE","subtitle":"Three gates today: the intent, the plan, the pull request. Same shape every time.","image":"human-gate.svg","imageAlt":"Agent output enters a gate where a human reviews the evidence, then accept or return; a dashed arrow returns to the agent.","imageCaption":"Nothing is written to a business system without this decision. Return always names the gap.","prompt":"Point at the gate. Say which three moments today are this gate, and that NEEDS REVISION always quotes a line.","steps":["Name the three gates of the day."],"expected":"Everyone can name the three gates.","check":"Nobody expects a step 2 on a NEEDS REVISION intent."},
{"title":"Human gate · step 1 · accept the boundary","kicker":"GATE · 11:00–11:10 · 10 MIN","subtitle":"No spec before the facilitator accepts the boundary","cards":[{"title":"Record","body":"Outcome sentence, the three checks, the boundary lines, the OPEN list"},{"title":"Decide","body":"ACCEPTED or NEEDS REVISION with one quoted line"},{"title":"Then","body":"Step 2 starts only from an accepted intent; compare with git diff step-1-intent -- intent.md"}],"prompt":"Pairs swap intents. Each reader quotes one line that makes the boundary safe and one line that is still a guess. The facilitator accepts or marks needs revision. Then everyone runs git diff step-1-intent -- intent.md and names one difference.","notes":"Eerste gate van de dag: de grens wordt geaccepteerd vóór er een spec komt. Laat paren elkaars intent lezen. Daarna diff met de tag: één verschil benoemen, niet overnemen.","dark":false,"steps":["Swap with a neighbour; quote one safe line and one guess.","Facilitator decides ACCEPTED / NEEDS REVISION.","Diff against step-1-intent; name one difference."],"expected":"An accepted intent per participant, one quoted line each.","check":"No step 2 work started on a NEEDS REVISION intent.","layout":"cards","tagline":"ACCEPT THE BOUNDARY FIRST · THEN THE SPEC"},
{"title":"Step 2 · the spec quotes the reference, the contract is code","kicker":"CONCEPT · SPEC · 11:10–11:20","subtitle":"docs/spec.md names every section with a quote from the PDFs; brief.ts is the same spec as a schema.","cards":[{"title":"The spec","body":"Seven sections in a fixed order, one quoted example per field, the house style, the never-do list."},{"title":"The contract","body":"BriefSchema in src/brief.ts: greeting, pushForward, todos, updates, day, notes. The model can only return that shape."},{"title":"The proof","body":"test/schema.test.ts: the sample passes, a brief without a push item fails, six top-level fields. Red first."}],"prompt":"Open docs/spec.md at step-2-spec next to the Tuesday PDF. Read the field table and find each example in the PDF. Then open brief.ts and match three describe() lines to three spec rows. Ask: which rule could the reference not settle? (The OPEN list.)","notes":"Spec = citaten uit de PDF, contract = dezelfde spec als code. Laat de groep drie describe()-regels aan drie spec-rijen koppelen. Wat de PDF niet beslist staat als OPEN.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• The spec: Seven sections in one fixed order, a table of fields with one quoted example each, the house style, what the agent may never do, acceptance examples with their proof command.\n• The contract: BriefSchema in src/brief.ts: greeting, pushForward, todos, updates, day, notes. It becomes the model's output schema, so the model can only return a shape the page knows.\n• The proof: test/schema.test.ts: the sample passes, a brief without a push item is rejected, the JSON schema carries exactly the six top-level fields. Red before the code exists.","dark":false,"steps":["Find three spec examples in the PDF.","Match three describe() lines to spec rows.","Read the spec's OPEN list."],"expected":"The room can say why the schema, not the prompt, is the contract.","check":"Every field in brief.ts has a row in spec.md with a quote.","layout":"cards"},
{"title":"Break","kicker":"BREAK · 11:20–11:35 · 15 MIN","subtitle":"Back at 11:35 for step 2 practice","cards":[{"title":"Goal","body":"Rest; leave the Tuesday PDF open"},{"title":"Mode","body":"Step 2 practice starts from the spec template"},{"title":"Boundary","body":"Nobody adds credentials during the break"}],"prompt":"Fifteen minutes. Leave the reference PDF and the spec template open so the next block starts from them.","notes":"Kwartier. Terug om 11:35.","dark":false,"steps":["Step away from the screen.","Back at 11:35."],"expected":"Everyone is back on time.","check":"One question about the contract is on the board."},
{"title":"Practice · step 2 · spec and contract, test first","kicker":"PRACTICE · 11:35–12:00 · 25 MIN · SOLO OR MOB","subtitle":"Card 2 · plan: fill docs/spec.md from the PDFs, then brief.ts, the sample and the schema tests","cards":[{"title":"Goal","body":"docs/spec.md with a quoted example per field; src/brief.ts; sample/brief.sample.json; test/schema.test.ts green"},{"title":"Input","body":"The two PDFs in reference/, the spec template, your accepted intent.md"},{"title":"Result","body":"npm test green on the schema tests; every field has a quoted spec row; the rest is OPEN."}],"prompt":"Read intent.md and the two PDFs in reference/. Fill docs/spec.md: the sections in order, a field table with one quoted example per field, the house style, what the agent may never do, and acceptance examples with their proof command. Then write test/schema.test.ts first (the sample must parse, a brief without a push item must be rejected), run npm test and show me the failure, and only then write src/brief.ts as a zod schema with describe() on every field and sample/brief.sample.json. Do not write a renderer, a tool or a prompt. Keep every rule the PDFs do not settle as OPEN.","notes":"25 minuten alleen. Volgorde: spec → rode test → schema + sample → groene test. Wie klaar is: `git diff step-2-spec --stat` en één verschil benoemen. Geen renderer, geen tools.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Result: npm test passes the schema tests; every field in brief.ts has a spec row with a quote; anything the PDFs do not settle is OPEN\n\nModus: individueel (ieder op my/<naam>) óf MOB (groepjes van 3–4, één driver, navigator wisselt elke 5–7 minuten, branch mob/<groep>). Kies per sessie; de stap, de tag en de check blijven gelijk.","dark":false,"steps":["Fill docs/spec.md with one quote per field.","Write test/schema.test.ts; run npm test; record the failure.","Write src/brief.ts and the sample; run npm test again.","Commit; diff against step-2-spec; name one difference."],"expected":"Schema tests green; spec rows with quotes; one named difference from the reference.","check":"The commit shows the test before brief.ts.","layout":"exercise","timer":25,"mascot":true,"tagline":"YOUR TURN · 25 MINUTES · QUOTE THE SOURCE · RED BEFORE GREEN"},
{"title":"Lunch","kicker":"LUNCH · 12:00–13:00","subtitle":"Back at 13:00 for design, the ADR and the plan","cards":[{"title":"Goal","body":"Rest"},{"title":"Mode","body":"The afternoon starts with the one decision that shaped the build"},{"title":"Boundary","body":"Nobody adds credentials during lunch"}],"prompt":"One hour. Leave your spec open; the afternoon starts from it.","notes":"Lunch. Terug om 13:00.","dark":false,"steps":["Back at 13:00."],"expected":"Everyone is back on time.","check":"Every spec is committed before lunch."},
{"title":"Lesson route · after lunch","kicker":"FIXED SCHEDULE · 13:00–16:00","subtitle":"The same route, halfway. Everything before lunch is behind us.","cards":[{"title":"Morning","body":"10:00–10:15 welcome · 10:15–10:35 concept: the loop · 10:35–11:10 step 1 intent · 11:10–11:20 step 2 spec · 11:20–11:35 break"},{"title":"Midday","body":"11:35–12:00 step 2 practice · 12:00–13:00 lunch · 13:00–13:25 step 3 design and plan · 13:25–14:00 step 4 render"},{"title":"Afternoon","body":"14:00–14:15 step 5 the loop · 14:15–14:30 break · 14:30–15:00 step 5 demo and tool · 15:00–15:20 hooks and evidence · 15:20–15:35 step 7 gate · 15:35–16:00 deploy, transfer, close"}],"prompt":"Show the same route again. Point at where the room is now, then name the artifact and the acceptance check for the afternoon steps.","notes":"Houd lunch en de twee pauzes vast; schuif de inhoud, niet de grenzen. Elke stap heeft een tag in de lab-repo: deelnemers vergelijken met `git diff step-N-… -- <bestand>`.","dark":false,"steps":["Point at where we are.","Name the next artifact.","Name its acceptance check."],"expected":"Everyone knows which steps remain and what each one has to produce.","check":"Everyone can name the next artifact and who accepts it.","layout":"cards","tagline":"SAME RHYTHM · CONCEPT FIRST · INDIVIDUAL AFTER · GATE BEFORE THE NEXT STEP"},
{"title":"Step 3 · design, one decision, a plan with proof","kicker":"CONCEPT · DESIGN · 13:00–13:10","subtitle":"design.md names the parts, ADR-001 records the one real choice, plan.md orders the build with a proof command per step.","cards":[{"title":"The contract","body":"brief.ts owns the shape, nothing else. Change a field and everything follows; change a source and nothing moves."},{"title":"The adapters","body":"sources.ts: one in-process tool server per system, every tool a bounded read-only GET. ADR-001: no browser OAuth."},{"title":"The checker","body":"render.ts escapes every model string; tests prove contract, sections and wiring; plan.md names the proof per step."}],"prompt":"Open docs/design.md at step-3-design: the parts table and the three boundaries (bound, watch, interrupt). Open ADR-001 and read the options table. Then open docs/plan.md and ask: which command proves step 4? Which gate sits before it?","notes":"Dezelfde drieslag als 'one contract, two platforms': contract, adapters, checker. Eén echte beslissing (ADR-001). Het plan heeft per stap een bewijscommando en een gate.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• The contract: brief.ts owns the shape and nothing else. Change a field and every other part follows; change a source and the contract does not move.\n• The adapters: sources.ts: one in-process tool server per system, each tool a bounded read-only GET. ADR-001 records why in-process instead of community MCP servers: no browser OAuth in a cron job.\n• The checker: render.ts escapes every model string; the tests prove the contract, the sections and the wiring. plan.md names which command proves each step and who accepts what before which step.","dark":false,"steps":["Read the parts table.","Read the ADR options table.","Find the proof command for step 4 in plan.md."],"expected":"The room can separate contract, adapter and checker and name the proof for the next step.","check":"Everyone can say which gate sits before the build.","layout":"cards"},
{"title":"Practice · step 3 · plan before acting","kicker":"PRACTICE · 13:10–13:25 · 15 MIN · SOLO OR MOB","subtitle":"Card 3 · design: fill docs/plan.md in read-only plan mode, proof command per step","cards":[{"title":"Goal","body":"docs/plan.md: ordered steps, exact paths, one proof command each, rollback, the human gate. One ADR."},{"title":"Input","body":"intent.md, docs/spec.md, the design template, the ADR template"},{"title":"Result","body":"A plan a stranger can follow that names what proves completion, accepted before step 4."}],"prompt":"In read-only plan mode, read intent.md and docs/spec.md. Draft docs/plan.md for the smallest slice that renders the sample brief to HTML without a credential: ordered steps with exact root-relative paths, one proof command per step, expected output, risks, rollback and the human gate before the build. Record one decision you made as docs/decisions/ADR-002.md. Do not write code and do not edit src/.","notes":"15 minuten alleen. Plan mode, geen code. Het plan wordt door de facilitator geaccepteerd vóór stap 4 begint. Eén ADR voor één echte keuze.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Goal: docs/plan.md with ordered steps, exact paths, one proof command each, rollback and the human gate; one ADR for a decision you made\n• Result: A plan a stranger can follow and that names what proves completion; accepted by the facilitator before step 4\n\nModus: individueel (ieder op my/<naam>) óf MOB (groepjes van 3–4, één driver, navigator wisselt elke 5–7 minuten, branch mob/<groep>). Kies per sessie; de stap, de tag en de check blijven gelijk.","dark":false,"steps":["Draft the ordered steps with paths and proof commands.","Write rollback and the human gate.","Record one decision as an ADR.","Ask the facilitator to accept the plan."],"expected":"An accepted plan.md and one ADR, committed.","check":"A stranger can name what proves each step from the plan alone.","layout":"exercise","timer":15,"mascot":true,"tagline":"YOUR TURN · 15 MINUTES · PLAN MODE · NO CODE"},
{"title":"Step 4 · render the sample, the first artifact","kicker":"DEMO · 13:25–13:35 · 10 MIN","subtitle":"render.ts is a pure function Brief → HTML; main.ts at this step only reads the sample","cards":[{"title":"Pure","body":"render.ts takes a Brief and returns a string. No dates, no fetching: string tests, no key needed."},{"title":"Escaped","body":"esc() on every model string. The test puts a script tag in the greeting; the page shows text."},{"title":"Styled from the source","body":"Yellow serif masthead, date rails, italic greeting, numbered updates, starburst, circled initials. Two languages, two themes, print."}],"prompt":"Run npm run brief:sample at step-4-build-render and open out/latest.html next to the Tuesday PDF. Walk the sections top to bottom. Then open render.ts and find esc(), the STRINGS table and the print block. Ask: what would break if the model returned markup?","notes":"Eerste artefact van de dag. Brief naast PDF. Wijs esc() aan en de test die het bewijst. Dit main.ts leest alleen de sample; stap 5 vervangt het.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Pure: render.ts takes a Brief and a RenderMeta and returns a string. No dates computed, no fetching, so the tests are string checks and the sample run needs no key.\n• Escaped: esc() on every model string. The test puts a script tag in the greeting and proves the page shows it as text.\n• Styled from the source: Yellow serif masthead, date and time rails, italic greeting, circles, numbered updates, the starburst, the circled initials. English and Dutch, light and dark, print.","dark":false,"steps":["Run the sample; open the page next to the PDF.","Find esc() and its test.","Name one difference from the PDF."],"expected":"Everyone has seen the sample render and knows where escaping lives.","check":"Everyone can say why the renderer needs no API key.","layout":"cards","tagline":"THE FIRST SLICE RENDERS WITHOUT A MODEL · THAT IS THE POINT"},
{"title":"Practice · step 4 · run it, change one rule, prove it","kicker":"PRACTICE · 13:35–14:00 · 25 MIN · SOLO OR MOB","subtitle":"Card 4 · build: render.ts and a sample-only main.ts on your branch, one house-style rule changed test-first","cards":[{"title":"Goal","body":"npm run brief:sample writes out/latest.html; one style rule changed with a test; a 1440×900 screenshot."},{"title":"Input","body":"Your brief.ts and sample; the render tests at step-4-build-render as a pattern; the PDFs"},{"title":"Result","body":"Render tests green; the page open next to the PDF; one difference recorded as OPEN"}],"prompt":"Following docs/plan.md, write src/render.ts as a pure function from my Brief to a self-contained HTML page in the style of the two PDFs, and a src/main.ts that only reads sample/brief.sample.json and writes out/latest.html. Work test-first: extend test/render.test.ts so every section title appears and a greeting containing <script> is escaped, run npm test and show me the failure, then implement. Do not fetch anything, do not add an agent or a tool. When it passes, change one house-style rule from docs/spec.md (for example the agenda time format) with its test first.","notes":"25 minuten alleen. Rode test eerst. Wie vastloopt: `git checkout step-4-build-render -- src/render.ts` en de diff lezen. Screenshot op 1440×900 bewaren voor stap 6.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Goal: npm run brief:sample writes out/latest.html from your contract; one style rule from your spec changed with a test; a screenshot at 1440×900\n\nModus: individueel (ieder op my/<naam>) óf MOB (groepjes van 3–4, één driver, navigator wisselt elke 5–7 minuten, branch mob/<groep>). Kies per sessie; de stap, de tag en de check blijven gelijk.","dark":false,"steps":["Write the render test; run npm test; record the failure.","Implement render.ts and the sample-only main.ts.","npm run brief:sample; open the page next to the PDF.","Change one style rule test-first.","Take the 1440×900 screenshot; commit."],"expected":"Render tests green; out/latest.html; one screenshot; one OPEN difference.","check":"The commit shows the test before the renderer.","layout":"exercise","timer":25,"mascot":true,"tagline":"YOUR TURN · 25 MINUTES · RED BEFORE GREEN · SCREENSHOT FOR STEP 6"},
{"title":"Step 5 · the loop inside query()","kicker":"CONCEPT · BUILD · 14:00–14:15","subtitle":"agent.ts is one call: bound the task, watch the loop, interrupt on purpose.","cards":[{"title":"BOUND THE TASK","body":"tools: [] removes every built-in tool; allowedTools lists only mcp__gitlab__* and friends; the prompt forbids invented facts."},{"title":"WATCH THE LOOP","body":"maxTurns caps the run; every tool call is logged; outputFormat validates against brief.ts; parseBrief() checks again."},{"title":"INTERRUPT ON PURPOSE","body":"permissionMode dontAsk: nothing pauses inside the run. The human interrupt is the pull request, after it."}],"prompt":"Open agent.ts at step-5-build-agent and read the options object line by line. For each line ask: bound, watch or interrupt? Then open sources.ts and read one tool: the typed view, clip(), guarded(). Ask why the human is not inside the loop. (A cron job that asks stalls forever.)","notes":"Zelfde drieslag als dag 4: bound, watch, interrupt. De mens zit ná de run, in de PR, niet erin. Eén tool lezen in sources.ts: typed view, clip, guarded.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• BOUND THE TASK: tools: [] removes every built-in tool; allowedTools lists only mcp__gitlab__* and friends; settingSources: [] keeps project settings out of a cron job; the system prompt says what a brief is and forbids invented facts.\n• WATCH THE LOOP: maxTurns caps the run; every tool call is logged with its input; outputFormat makes the SDK validate the answer against brief.ts and retry on its own; parseBrief() checks it again.\n• INTERRUPT ON PURPOSE: permissionMode dontAsk: nothing pauses for a human inside the run. The human interrupt sits after it: the pull request, and the reader who decides what to push.","dark":false,"steps":["Classify each option: bound, watch or interrupt.","Read one tool in sources.ts.","Say where the human sits and why."],"expected":"The room can read agent.ts as a bounded loop with the human after it.","check":"Nobody puts a human approval prompt inside the scheduled run.","layout":"cards"},
{"dark":false,"layout":"image","cards":[],"notes":"Herhaling in beeld. Wijs het plaatje aan en laat de groep het concept in één zin zeggen.","title":"The agentic loop · see the loop","kicker":"VISUAL · AGENTIC LOOP","subtitle":"One query(): gather, act, verify, until the schema is met. The human sits after the loop.","image":"agentic-loop.svg","imageAlt":"Your prompt enters a loop of gather, act and verify that repeats until done; a human box can interrupt, steer or add context at any point.","imageCaption":"Models reason, tools act, the platform holds the loop. The loop ends at a human gate, never at \"done\" by itself.","prompt":"Point at gather, act and verify, then at where this agent puts the human: the pull request, after the run.","steps":["Point at where the human sits for this agent."],"expected":"Everyone can place the pull request on the picture.","check":"Nobody expects an approval prompt inside the scheduled run."},
{"title":"Break","kicker":"BREAK · 14:15–14:30 · 15 MIN","subtitle":"Back at 14:30 for the demo run","cards":[{"title":"Goal","body":"Rest; leave agent.ts open"},{"title":"Mode","body":"The demo run reads a saved transcript if the room has no network"},{"title":"Boundary","body":"Nobody adds credentials during the break"}],"prompt":"Fifteen minutes. Leave agent.ts open so the demo starts from it.","notes":"Kwartier. Terug om 14:30.","dark":false,"steps":["Step away from the screen.","Back at 14:30."],"expected":"Everyone is back on time.","check":"One question about the loop is on the board."},
{"title":"Trainer demo · step 5 · one run, read the transcript","kicker":"DEMO · 14:30–14:40 · 10 MIN","subtitle":"Gather, act, verify: the three phases of the agentic loop, visible in the stderr log","cards":[{"title":"Gather","body":"The first turn calls the survey tools in parallel: to-dos, merge requests, issues, pages, today's calendar."},{"title":"Act","body":"The next turns drill into at most four items whose state decides the ranking."},{"title":"Verify","body":"The SDK checks the JSON against the schema; parseBrief() checks again; render.ts escapes it. Then a file."}],"prompt":"Run npm run brief with the trainer's sandbox token for one source, or replay the saved stderr log from LESSON.md if there is no network. Read the tool calls aloud as they appear and name the phase of each: gather, act, verify. Stop at the result line and point at turns and cost.","notes":"Zonder netwerk: speel het opgeslagen log af (LESSON.md). Benoem per tool-call de fase. Wijs de kosten aan: dit is een dagelijkse run, dus dit getal telt.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Gather: The first turn calls the survey tools in parallel: to-dos, open merge requests, open issues, recent pages, today's calendar\n• Act: The next turns drill into at most four items whose state decides the ranking: an MR with unresolved threads, an issue with a fresh comment\n• Verify: The SDK checks the final JSON against the schema; parseBrief() checks it again; render.ts escapes it. Only then is a file written","dark":false,"steps":["Start the run; watch the first parallel calls.","Name the phase of each call.","Stop at the result line; read turns and cost."],"expected":"Everyone has seen gather, act and verify in one real transcript.","check":"Everyone can say what happens if the model returns a brief that does not match the schema.","layout":"cards","tagline":"MODELS REASON · TOOLS ACT · THE SCHEMA VERIFIES · THE PR DECIDES"},
{"title":"Practice · step 5 · add one read-only tool","kicker":"PRACTICE · 14:40–15:00 · 20 MIN · SOLO OR MOB","subtitle":"Card 5 · build: take sources.ts and agent.ts from the tag, then add one tool, wiring proven by a test","cards":[{"title":"Goal","body":"sources.ts and agent.ts on your branch, plus one new read-only tool the model can call."},{"title":"Input","body":"git checkout step-5-build-agent -- src/sources.ts src/agent.ts src/main.ts test/agent.test.ts; the tool() + guarded() pattern"},{"title":"Result","body":"The tool listed in its server, covered by the allow-list, a wiring test; typecheck and tests green."}],"prompt":"Take src/sources.ts, src/agent.ts, src/main.ts and test/agent.test.ts from the tag step-5-build-agent. Then add a read-only tool [gitlab_failed_pipelines] to the [gitlab] server in src/sources.ts, following the existing tool() + guarded() pattern with a typed view, clipped strings and a bounded list. Extend test/agent.test.ts so the wiring is proven without a network call. Keep the allow-list wildcard as it is and do not add write access of any kind. Show me npm test and npm run typecheck.","notes":"20 minuten alleen. Eerst de tag-bestanden overnemen (dat is het bewuste 'catch up'-moment), dan één tool. Geen schrijfrechten, geen credentials. Wie klaar is: in één zin wat de tool teruggeeft en waarom dat begrensd is.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Goal: sources.ts and agent.ts on your branch, plus one new read-only tool (for example gitlab_failed_pipelines or outlook_tomorrow) the model can call\n• Result: The tool listed in its server, covered by mcp__<source>__*, a test that proves the wiring; typecheck and tests green; no live call needed\n\nModus: individueel (ieder op my/<naam>) óf MOB (groepjes van 3–4, één driver, navigator wisselt elke 5–7 minuten, branch mob/<groep>). Kies per sessie; de stap, de tag en de check blijven gelijk.","dark":false,"steps":["Take the four files from step-5-build-agent.","Pick the source and the question the tool answers.","Copy the tool() + guarded() pattern; bound the output.","Prove the wiring in the test.","Run npm test and npm run typecheck; commit."],"expected":"One new tool, typecheck and tests green, output bounded.","check":"The new tool has no more access than its question needs.","layout":"exercise","timer":20,"mascot":true,"tagline":"YOUR TURN · 20 MINUTES · READ-ONLY BY CONSTRUCTION"},
{"title":"Hooks · where the guardrails hold","kicker":"CONCEPT · HOOKS · 15:00–15:05","subtitle":"The prompt advises; three pieces of code hold without exception.","cards":[{"title":"SKILL VS HOOK","body":"\"Never invent facts\" in the prompt is advisory. tools: [] and read-only scopes are deterministic."},{"title":"WHERE IT FIRES","body":"guarded() wraps every tool: a failing API becomes a tool error, not a crash. esc() on every string."},{"title":"WHAT IT DOES","body":"Blocks writes by construction, keeps a dead source honest, keeps model text out of markup. Review stays outside."}],"prompt":"Ask: which rule in the system prompt must hold even if the model ignores the prompt? Then point at the code that holds it. Collect the three on the board: tools: [], guarded(), esc(). Then ask what does not belong inside the run. (npm test, the human approval.)","notes":"Zelfde definitie als dag 5: advisory versus deterministisch. Laat de groep de regel uit de prompt aanwijzen en dan de code die hem afdwingt. De tabel staat in docs/design.md.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• SKILL VS HOOK: The system prompt says \"never invent facts\". That is advisory. tools: [] and the read-only token scopes are the deterministic layer: the model has nothing to write with.\n• WHERE IT FIRES: guarded() wraps every tool so a failing API becomes a tool error the model reports, not a crashed run. esc() runs on every string before it reaches the page.\n• WHAT IT DOES: Blocks writes by construction, keeps a dead source honest, keeps model text from becoming markup. The full test suite and the human review stay outside the run.","dark":false,"steps":["Name one prompt rule that must hold without exception.","Point at the code that holds it."],"expected":"The room can separate advisory from deterministic on this agent.","check":"Nobody names the prompt as the thing that prevents a write.","layout":"cards"},
{"dark":false,"layout":"image","cards":[],"notes":"Herhaling in beeld. Wijs het plaatje aan en laat de groep het concept in één zin zeggen.","title":"Hooks · see the guardrail","kicker":"VISUAL · HOOKS","subtitle":"The prompt advises; tools: [], guarded() and esc() hold.","image":"hooks-guardrails.svg","imageAlt":"A skill feeds a hook box; each action leaves as block, fix or allow. Below, build, commit/PR and deploy show where hooks, the test suite and human approval live.","imageCaption":"Hooks live in the build. The full test suite belongs at the commit or PR. Human approval belongs at the deploy gate.","prompt":"Point at block, fix, allow. Then name the three pieces of code in this agent that hold without exception.","steps":["Name the three pieces of code that hold."],"expected":"Everyone can name tools: [], guarded() and esc().","check":"Nobody thinks the prompt is what prevents a write."},
{"title":"Practice · step 6 · record the evidence","kicker":"PRACTICE · 15:05–15:20 · 15 MIN · SOLO OR MOB","subtitle":"Card 6 · test: docs/evidence.md with three commands, exit codes, one screenshot and a reviewer","cards":[{"title":"Goal","body":"docs/evidence.md: one row per command with exit code, quoted output and the neighbour who reran it; the screenshot."},{"title":"Input","body":"npm run typecheck, npm test, npm run brief:sample; the screenshot from step 4; the evidence template"},{"title":"Result","body":"No row without a reviewer; every difference from the PDFs as OPEN; committed"}],"prompt":"Run npm run typecheck, npm test and npm run brief:sample in this repository and fill docs/evidence.md: one row per command with the exit code, one quoted output line, and the reviewer column left for a person. Copy the 1440×900 screenshot to docs/evidence/ and describe it. List every difference from the reference PDFs as OPEN. Do not write PASS anywhere and do not invent a reviewer.","notes":"15 minuten alleen. Drie commando's, één screenshot, één bewijsregel per commando. Een buur herhaalt één commando en tekent als reviewer. Verschillen met de PDF zijn OPEN, geen fout. Claude vult de rijen, de mens tekent.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Goal: docs/evidence.md filled: one row per command with the exit code you saw, the quoted output line and the neighbour who reran it; the 1440×900 screenshot under docs/evidence/\n\nModus: individueel (ieder op my/<naam>) óf MOB (groepjes van 3–4, één driver, navigator wisselt elke 5–7 minuten, branch mob/<groep>). Kies per sessie; de stap, de tag en de check blijven gelijk.","dark":false,"steps":["Run the three commands; record exit codes.","Fill the rows with one quoted output line each.","Copy and describe the screenshot.","Have a neighbour rerun one command and sign as reviewer.","Commit."],"expected":"Three evidence rows with exit codes, one screenshot, one reviewer signature.","check":"No row claims a command nobody ran.","layout":"exercise","timer":15,"mascot":true,"tagline":"YOUR TURN · 15 MINUTES · CLAIM · SOURCE + CHECK · REVIEWER"},
{"title":"Human gate · step 7 · the pull request","kicker":"GATE · 15:20–15:35 · 15 MIN","subtitle":"CI and the review bot do the first pass; a person reads the diff against intent.md and decides.","cards":[{"title":"Record","body":"Branch, three commands with exit codes, the screenshot, the new tool's name; what each check observed."},{"title":"Decide","body":"PASS / FAIL / OPEN with one quoted line from the diff or the intent, in docs/gate.md"},{"title":"Then","body":"Merge, or send it back with the quoted line; the schedule in gitlab-ci.example.yml starts only after a PASS"}],"prompt":"Open a merge request from my/<name> and swap with a neighbour. Read the checks first and say what each observed. Then read the diff against intent.md: which success check does it prove, which boundary does it touch? Fill docs/gate.md with PASS / FAIL / OPEN and one quoted line, and the handoff block for the person who takes it next.","notes":"Een groen vinkje is een observatie, geen goedkeuring. De mens leest de diff tegen intent.md. OPEN mag: 'niet gedraaid tegen een echte bron' is een eerlijke uitkomst. Het handoff-blok is voor de collega die het overneemt.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Record: Branch, the three commands with exit codes, the screenshot, the new tool's name; what each automated check actually observed","dark":false,"steps":["Open the merge request; swap with a neighbour.","Read the checks; say what each observed.","Read the diff against intent.md.","Fill gate.md: PASS / FAIL / OPEN with a quoted line, and the handoff."],"expected":"A gate.md per participant with a decision, a quoted line and a named receiver.","check":"No PASS rests on a check nobody read.","layout":"cards","tagline":"A GREEN CHECK IS AN OBSERVATION · THE MERGE IS A DECISION"},
{"title":"Deploy and maintain · close the loop","kicker":"CONCEPT · DEPLOY · 15:35–15:40","subtitle":"A schedule is the deploy; the notes footnote is the maintenance signal; tomorrow's brief is the next plan.","cards":[{"title":"Deploy","body":"One cron line or a GitLab scheduled pipeline. Credentials in CI variables, never in the repo."},{"title":"Maintain","body":"Every brief ends with notes: a failed source, an empty window, an assumption. Repeats become tickets."},{"title":"Learn","body":"Tomorrow's run reads today's merge and the ticket a footnote became. That is the loop closing."}],"prompt":"Show gitlab-ci.example.yml and the cron line. Ask: what would you watch in the first week, and which footnote would make you change intent.md? That answer is the loop closing.","notes":"Deploy is hier klein: één regel cron. Maintain is het lezen van de voetnoten. Vraag welke voetnoot de intent zou veranderen: dat is de lus.\n\nVolledige kaarttekst (van de slide gehaald, hier voor de facilitator):\n• Deploy: One cron line or a GitLab scheduled pipeline (gitlab-ci.example.yml). Credentials live in CI variables, never in the repo. The run writes a file, nothing else.\n• Maintain: Every brief ends with notes: a source that failed, an empty window, an assumption. Read them like a log; the one that repeats becomes a ticket and a line in progress.md.\n• Learn: Tomorrow's run reads today's merge, the ticket that footnote became, and the meeting it caused. When a footnote changes intent.md, the loop has closed.","dark":false,"steps":["Show the schedule.","Read one notes footnote from the sample.","Say which footnote would change intent.md."],"expected":"Everyone can name the artifact of deploy and the signal of maintain.","check":"Deploy is described as a schedule and a file, never as a service that acts on its own.","layout":"cards","tagline":"A CRON LINE IS A DEPLOY · A FOOTNOTE IS A MAINTENANCE SIGNAL"},
{"title":"MOB transfer · which brief would your team read?","kicker":"TRANSFER · 15:40–15:50 · 10 MIN","subtitle":"One intent from the morning, one source to start with, one human decision that stays","cards":[{"title":"Intent","body":"From the intents accepted at 11:00: which one gets a first live run next week?"},{"title":"First source","body":"The single source that gives the most leverage with the least access, and the token scope it needs"},{"title":"Stays human","body":"The one decision no footnote and no schedule may take"}],"prompt":"As a MOB, pick one intent from the room. Name the first source to connect, the token scope it needs, the person who owns the gate, and the decision that stays human whatever the brief says. Write it on the board as OPEN items where the room does not know.","notes":"MOB: één intent kiezen, één bron, één eigenaar van de gate. Alles wat de groep niet weet staat als OPEN op het bord. Geen beloftes over toegang die er nog niet is.","dark":false,"steps":["Pick one intent.","Name the first source and its scope.","Name the gate owner.","Name the decision that stays human."],"expected":"One board with intent, source, scope, owner and the human decision.","check":"No access is promised that nobody in the room can grant.","tagline":"ONE INTENT · ONE SOURCE · ONE OWNER · ONE HUMAN DECISION"},
{"dark":false,"layout":"image","cards":[],"notes":"Herhaling in beeld. Wijs het plaatje aan en laat de groep het concept in één zin zeggen.","title":"The brief on the loop · recap","kicker":"RECAP · AI-NATIVE SDLC","subtitle":"The same picture as this morning. Now every box is a file on your branch.","image":"daily-brief-on-the-loop.svg","imageAlt":"Six phases on an orange loop, each with the daily brief agent's documents and files: intent, spec and plan; design, ADR and brief.ts; render, sources and agent; npm test, the sample run and evidence.md; gate.md, the merged PR and a schedule; the notes footnote and progress.md. Two orange human gates and one purple hook point sit on the loop around the Claude Agent SDK.","imageCaption":"Seven steps, seven files, three gates and one hook point. Say each step in one sentence.","prompt":"Point at each phase and let the room name the file it produced today, before the recap slide asks for the sentences.","steps":["Name the file for each phase."],"expected":"Every phase has a file someone can point at.","check":"No phase is named without a file."},
{"title":"Recap","kicker":"RECAP · 15:50–15:55","subtitle":"One sentence per step, from the room, pointing at a file","cards":[],"prompt":"Ask the room to finish each sentence and point at the file or the evidence row that proves it.","notes":"Eén zin per stap, met een bestand erbij. Geen zin zonder bewijs.","dark":false,"steps":["Ask for intent and spec.","Ask for design, plan and render.","Ask for the loop and the evidence.","Ask for the gate; point at the files."],"expected":"Seven sentences on the board that each point at a file.","check":"No sentence claims an unobserved result.","layout":"recap","items":[{"label":"The intent was…","caption":"intent.md: outcome, success checks, boundary, OPEN, accepted before the spec"},{"label":"The spec and contract are…","caption":"docs/spec.md quoting the PDFs and brief.ts, the same thing as code, tested first"},{"label":"The design and plan were…","caption":"design.md, one ADR, plan.md with a proof command and a gate per step"},{"label":"The first artifact was…","caption":"render.ts on the sample: a page without a model, escaped"},{"label":"The loop is…","caption":"one query() with read-only tools, bounded, watched, the human after it"},{"label":"The evidence was…","caption":"three commands with exit codes, one screenshot, one reviewer who reran"},{"label":"The gate was…","caption":"gate.md: the PR read against intent.md, PASS / FAIL / OPEN with a quoted line"}],"tagline":"SEVEN STEPS · SEVEN FILES · EVIDENCE, NOT FEELINGS"},
{"title":"Check-out and reflection","kicker":"CLOSE · 15:55–16:00","subtitle":"Made, learned, can do — then one OPEN item each","cards":[{"title":"Individual","body":"Made / Learned / Can do"},{"title":"OPEN","body":"One thing you would need to see before trusting the brief"},{"title":"Next","body":"The first live run, on one source, behind a human gate"}],"prompt":"Each person writes Made, Learned, Can do, and one OPEN item they would need to see before trusting the brief. Update progress.md on your branch with observed results only.","notes":"Persoonlijke scores blijven privé. Eén OPEN per persoon: wat moet je zien voordat je de brief vertrouwt? progress.md alleen met waargenomen resultaten.","dark":true,"steps":["Made / Learned / Can do.","One OPEN per person.","Update progress.md; commit."],"expected":"A truthful close with one OPEN item per person and a progress.md that matches the branch.","check":"Every uncertainty is sourced or OPEN.","layout":"cards","tagline":"PREPARE · APPROVE · EXECUTE · ESCALATE WHEN AUTHORITY OR EVIDENCE IS MISSING"}
]}};
